00:07:01.110 --> 00:07:05.920
So I come from a
heavy Excel background.

00:07:05.920 --> 00:07:10.460
So I will caveat my
response by saying

00:07:10.460 --> 00:07:14.130
my views might be a little
more nuanced than someone

00:07:14.130 --> 00:07:17.410
may be coming from a CS
background or someone--

00:07:17.410 --> 00:07:19.410
especially nowadays,
I feel like people

00:07:19.410 --> 00:07:22.320
graduating from undergrad and
going into master's programs

00:07:22.320 --> 00:07:26.370
or diving straight into machine
learning, which is awesome.

00:07:26.370 --> 00:07:33.210
But I will say there is
a lot of reporting or KPI

00:07:33.210 --> 00:07:40.200
creation or evaluating different
KPIs that doesn't require

00:07:40.200 --> 00:07:43.680
machine learning and that is
also high value, because it

00:07:43.680 --> 00:07:47.280
helps the business
track whether or not

00:07:47.280 --> 00:07:53.280
some different product
or program is successful.

00:07:53.280 --> 00:07:59.650
Where, machine
learning can be used

00:07:59.650 --> 00:08:02.560
for inference or prediction.

00:08:02.560 --> 00:08:06.730
And I feel like
both kind of sides

00:08:06.730 --> 00:08:08.830
of this machine-learning
equation

00:08:08.830 --> 00:08:12.350
add a lot of value
for different reasons.

00:08:12.350 --> 00:08:17.800
When it gets to
prediction, I'd say

00:08:17.800 --> 00:08:22.450
this is where you
really want to make

00:08:22.450 --> 00:08:25.870
an intervention of
some sort, or you

00:08:25.870 --> 00:08:28.780
want to focus on a subset
of your overall customers

00:08:28.780 --> 00:08:32.650
or consumers and either
give value to them

00:08:32.650 --> 00:08:40.400
or help the business maybe by
mitigating the risk of churn.

00:08:40.400 --> 00:08:41.650
There's just a lot of reasons.

00:08:41.650 --> 00:08:43.240
I'm not giving a
great answer here,

00:08:43.240 --> 00:08:45.100
